    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part26/6/6/8~3",
      "quote": "In the Opposed Word Trade Mark there is no accompanying device to aid potential purchasers in distinguishing between it and the Opponent’s Registered Trade Mark. Deception or confusion is therefore likely to arise out of the use of the Opposed Word Trade Mark (at [77]) I therefore find that the Opposed Word Trade Mark is deceptively similar to the Opponent’s Registered Trade Mark but that the Opposed Logo Trade Mark is not deceptively similar to the Opponent’s Registered Trade Mark (at [78])"
